                  <msItem>
                     <title>Missale</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Ed. D.H. Turner, The Missal of the New Minster,
                        Winchester, HBS 93 (1962); reduced facs. of fol. 62r, see pp. viii--xiiii.
                        Turner says "Stowe 2 and Le Havre 330 seem to have a scribe or scribes in
                        common" (p. xi).</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">For older literature, see L. Delisle and C.
                        Fierville in Rev. des sociétés savantes, 7eme série, 6 (1882) p. 33, with
                        facsimiles; Mémoires de la Soc. havraise d'études diverses (1880--1881), pp.
                        401--546, and V. Leroquais, Les sacramentaires et les Milssels, 1. 190.
                        These suggest that the liturgy points to either Winchester (St Swithun) or
                        Hyde and, in MLGB2, this manuscript was attributed to Winchester, but that
                        was rejected and the volume re-assigned to Hyde in the Supplement.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
